# Sparky Stereo OS, an edition of SparkyLinux.
# new-lg4ff (berarma/new-lg4ff, revision 2092db1) ships no udev rules. Its
# sysfs files (range, gain, autocenter, effect levels, LEDs) are created
# root:root with mode 0664, so only root can set them. This edition rule gives
# them the convention hid-fanatecff's own rules use: group "games", group-
# writable; nothing is opened to other users. TEST=="range" limits it to the
# wheels the driver gives force feedback (the replaced hid-logitech module also
# binds keyboards and mice). real_id is read-only in the driver and is left
# alone. The hidraw node comes from sparky-sim-hidraw (uaccess). The helper skips a control
# the model does not have and says, through sparky-stereo-problems, one it has and cannot
# set (sparky-stereo-wheel-access). See README.Debian.
ACTION!="add|change|bind", GOTO="sparky_lg4ff_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="hid", DRIVER=="logitech", TEST=="range", RUN+="/usr/lib/udev/sparky-stereo-wheel-access --mode g+w new-lg4ff %S%p alternate_modes autocenter combine_pedals damper_level ffb_leds friction_level gain peak_ffb_level range spring_level"
LABEL="sparky_lg4ff_end"
